# Switch rate

**What this is.** Number of ancestry switches per haplotype on this
chromosome. Pure-ancestry haplotypes sit near zero; recently admixed
haplotypes spread to dozens. Outliers in the 100+ tail are typically
driven by phasing errors or LAI noise rather than real biology.

**How to read this chart.** The bold top row is the cohort — the
horizontal line spans cohort `min` to cohort `p99`, the vertical
blue tick is the n_haplotypes-weighted mean, the hollow square is
the n-weighted median, and the red ✕ is the cohort-wide max. The dim
rows below show the same forest for each cluster · chrom. Read the
cohort row first; if the per-cluster rows are tightly bunched around
it, the cohort number is stable. A cluster whose ✕ jumps far past
its own p99 has at least one haplotype with pathological switching
worth pulling out.

